  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking shows federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, with a reported total of $197B in obligations across the listed contractors. The table lists the ten largest contractors by obligations for the fiscal year to date. FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO leads the list with $13.4B in obligations, followed by TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $12.6B and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $10B. Other large obligations include MCKESSON CORPORATION at $9.9B, a second LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION entry at $9.2B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $8.5B, OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. at $6.6B, RAYTHEON COMPANY at $6.3B, BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED at $5.9B, and THE BOEING COMPANY at $5.9B. The report notes that all figures are contract obligations and that current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date reporting.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What does the $197B total represent?",
        "body": "The $197B total represents contract obligations for FY2026 to date. All figures shown are contract obligations. The note clarifies that current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date reporting. This total aggregates obligations across the listed contractors."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which companies top the list and what are their obligations?",
        "body": "FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO tops the list with $13.4B in obligations. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is second at $12.6B, followed by LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $10B and MCKESSON CORPORATION at $9.9B. The list also includes a second LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION entry at $9.2B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $8.5B, OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. at $6.6B, RAYTHEON COMPANY at $6.3B, BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED at $5.9B, and THE BOEING COMPANY at $5.9B."
      }
    ]
